---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';
---

<Base title="Colophon" description="How joshhorn.net is built: Astro, plain CSS, and very little JavaScript.">
  <PageIntro title="Colophon">
    <p>Notes on how this site is put together, for anyone who cares about that sort of thing.</p>
  </PageIntro>

  <section class="row">
    <h2 class="label">Build</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Built with <a href="https://astro.build" rel="noopener">Astro</a> and shipped as static HTML. There is
        no front-end framework. The only JavaScript on the site is the theme switch, the print button on
        the Experience page, and the X12 explorer on the EDI case study, and every page works without it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Content lives in a few typed data files, so updating a job or a service never means touching
        markup.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="row">
    <h2 class="label">Design</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Headings are set in Newsreader and body text in Public Sans, both self-hosted. The layout borrows
        from printed résumés: a narrow column of labels, a wide column of content, and hairline rules
        between sections.
      </p>
      <p>
        Colors are a handful of CSS custom properties with a light and a dark set; the site follows your
        system setting unless you pick one in the footer. Page-to-page transitions use the CSS View
        Transitions API, and they turn off if you've asked your system to reduce motion.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="row">
    <h2 class="label">Details</h2>
    <ul class="prose list">
      <li>Every page has a print stylesheet. The Experience page prints as a résumé.</li>
      <li>The EDI flow diagram is HTML and CSS rather than an image, so it reflows on small screens.</li>
      <li>Focus styles are visible, and every interactive element works from the keyboard.</li>
      <li>Layouts are checked at phone, tablet, and desktop widths in both color themes.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="row">
    <h2 class="label">Hosting</h2>
    <p class="prose">Deployed on Cloudflare from the main branch on every push.</p>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .list {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.6rem;
  }

  .list li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1.1rem;
  }

  .list li::before {
    content: '–';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--ink-3);
  }
</style>
